  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe embedded catalog now includes 22 generic router cutters.\nThe existing library picker offers them without a separate file.\n\n- Up-cut, down-cut, compression and ball nose tools: 3 mm, 6 mm, 1/8 in and 1/4 in.\n- Sharp-point V-bits: 60 and 90 degrees, with 6 mm and 1/4 in shanks.\n- Surfacing bits: 25 mm and 1 in. These tools cannot plunge through their centre.\n\nEach entry states its flute length and exposed shank length.\nTheir sum gives the modeled stick-out.\nThe inch sizes use exact mm conversions.\nThe existing tools keep their values and relative order.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/3069-router-starter-tools.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe starter catalog had no router set.\nUsers had to define these common cutters before they could select them.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `catalog_asset_tests::router_starter_tools_state_their_shapes_and_reach` pins all 22 names, shapes, dimensions, reach and baseline values.\n- `router_starter_library_imports_without_refusals_and_undoes_as_one_unit` pins import, exact definitions, undo and redo.\n- Both pins failed before the asset changed. Each found 0 router tools instead of 22.\n- Mutation: restore `assets/tools/catalog.json` from `upstream/main`. Both pins fail. Restore the fixed asset. Both pins pass.\n- The legacy catalog test still checks the old tool order. It also checks all tools for validity.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed on the final code. It ran 101 tools tests and 15 app tests.\n- `cargo clippy -j6 -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` passed: 236 steps, 0 failed, 38 minutes.\n- Motion heavy lane: 59 tests passed. Two known-fail checks matched #1950.\n- App heavy lane: 43 tests passed. Four known-fail checks matched #1950 and #2849.\n- The [latest review](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/3159#issuecomment-7063067027) supplies these local heavy results on head `5bb177e5247ad6ebc3bc4148bd1935a63d6934ec`. No source changed after that review.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe GUI and a real machine were not exercised.\nThe existing picker reads the embedded catalog.\nThe cutter and holder dimensions are nominal. Check them against the actual assembly before machining.\nThe positive speed and feed values satisfy the existing reader. They are not verified settings for a real cut.\nMaterial-specific wood cutting rows wait for #3068 and PR #3158.\nThe names identify cut direction. The model does not store a compression transition height.\nThese V-bits have sharp points. Flat-tip support stays with #895.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2714 touches the same catalog file, different tool entries. It extends the `ORDER` constant in the test file. This PR changes `the_shipped_asset_parses_and_every_tool_is_valid` and adds a separate pin. It keeps that constant intact.\n- #2836 touches the same catalog file, different tool entries.\n\nEach touches the same file, different function or row; whichever merges second refreshes.\nNo open PR changes the lines changed here. This PR does not need a stack.\n\nEffort: medium. The issue did not escalate.\n\nChangelog: Add a generic starter router tool set in inch and metric sizes, with stated flute lengths and stick-out.\n\nFixes #3069\n",
